# Aria

Local, privacy-first voice assistant: a Rust daemon, its CLI, the macOS app,
and the speech toolkit crates they are built from.

## Commands

Run from the repository root. `justfile` owns commands; Cargo manifests own
package names and engine features. `just check` enables all features on
macOS. The scoped recipes use default features.

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Gate, before committing | `just check` = `proto-check` + `rust-native` + `support-check` |
| Check then lint one package, while editing | `just rust-check <package>`, `just rust-lint <package>` |
| Test one package | `just rust-test <package> [filter]` |
| Rust part of the gate, every package | `just rust-native` |
| Shell and sidecar part of the gate | `just support-check` |
| macOS app formatting and tests | `just swift-check` |
| Build `Aria.app` with the daemon inside | `just app` |
| Affected cross-target gate | `just rust-wasm` / `just rust-linux` |
| Build the CLI | `cargo build --release --bin aria` |
| Build / serve books | `just book` / `just book-serve` |

## Runtime Pitfalls

- The source-built CLI is `target/release/aria`. A running daemon outlives a
  rebuild; restart it using the intended binary before checking live behavior.
- `aria config show` reflects the invoking shell. The service has its own
  environment; restart it after changing `~/.aria/config.yaml`.
- Keep immutable daemon configuration, daemon-owned shared preferences, and
  client-local presentation choices separate. Reject unknown configuration keys.
- Listen transcription and voice tracking read separate
  `RecordingReader::fork()` readers. Preserve the lag and drain bounds in
  `crates/aria/src/listen/track.rs`.
- Setup, model downloads, recording, installation, and service changes have
  side effects. Validate documentation with help output and dry-runs.

## macOS App

- Edit `clients/project.yml`, then run `just swift-project`; keep personal signing
  in ignored `clients/project.local.yml`. Regenerate protocol stubs with
  `just proto-swift`; never hand-edit `clients/Generated/`.
- Preserve Swift 6 mode; get approval for per-target opt-outs. Keep UI state on
  `@MainActor` and explicitly hop there from off-main callbacks.
- Explain the safety invariant for every `nonisolated(unsafe)` or
  `@unchecked Sendable` use.
- Never log audio or transcripts; mark log values `.public` only if nonpersonal.
  Show plain error messages to users; avoid force-unwraps, `try!`, and
  `fatalError` in production paths.
- Keep decision logic separate from OS effects so XCTest can cover it without
  live audio, sockets, or devices. Add protocols only for actual substitution.
- Use `just swift-fix` for formatting.

## Tests

- Rust unit tests live beside their modules; integration tests live in each
  Cargo package's `tests/`. Keep fixtures with their consuming package.
- The optional Python sidecar uses `uv` without a root Python project or
  activated environment. `just support-check` runs its checks.

## Licensing

- `crates/aria`, `crates/aria-bench`, and the macOS app are GPL-3.0-only. The
  library crates and `proto/` are Apache-2.0; keep `crates/aria` out of their
  dependencies.
- Files that draw the Aria logo fall under `assets/brand/LICENSE`, not GPL.
  List any new one there and give it the same header.
- Record copied third-party files in `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`. If the file
  ships in a published crate, add the notice to that crate's own
  `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` too.

## Maintaining Instructions

- Add rules only for recurring, non-obvious mistakes, with a concrete action.
- Scope rules to the work they affect. Link to detailed references; leave file
  inventories and API descriptions to the code.
- During feature or fix work, suggest rule additions for review instead of
  editing instructions incidentally.
- Edit `.rules`. `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are symlinks to it.
